      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The schoolhouse’s upper floor earned the nickname “The Tabernacle” after hosting Baptist, Reformed Dutch, and Methodist meetings before a dedicated church was built in 1854.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bellvale%2C_New_York",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bellvale lies along New York State Route 17A, while Pumpkin Hill Road follows the historic Tuxedo‑to‑Warwick road improved by Continental Army engineers in 1779.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bellvale%2C_New_York",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The original iron forge built by Lawrence Scrauley in 1745 was the colony’s first water‑wheel‑powered mill, but British soldiers destroyed it in 1750.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bellvale%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Long House Creek powered a chain of mills that, by 1775, helped forge the 188‑ton chain blocking the Hudson at West Point during the Revolution.",
